Subject: [PATCH] spa: libcamera: Honour the negotiated capture format

CameraConfiguration::validate() may adjust the pixel format or size.
Reporting the requested fields after that adjustment gives the client a
format different from the buffers returned by the camera.

Reject changes to an exact request. When NEAREST permits an adjustment
within the same media subtype, signal the change and return the accepted
format so the video adapter can negotiate with the actual buffer layout.

Check explicit DMA-BUF modifiers against the validated or running pixel
format. Fixate modifier choices only when they contain that exact layout
and report explicit linear selections as zero. Linear buffers can still
match clients that do not negotiate a modifier.

diff --git a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp
--- a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp
+++ b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp
